e 'UX/UI' or 'web design' chapter — the coverage appears woven into the introduction and framing prose (and likely the Exhibits) rather than being a dedicated new structural section with named web-specific techniques. So 'expanded coverage' is accurate but should not be overread as a full dedicated web-design chapter; it's real, explicit, substantive commentary, not a token mention. (3) Source quality — upgraded well beyond the original Tier-C marketing-copy citation: I independently verified with the book's actual primary text. (4) Not outdated — 2023 edition, current. (5) Not marketing fluff on inspection — the marketing copy's claim is corroborated by the primary source itself.",
